CSS:
   -> stand for cascading style sheet  
   -> used increase standards and overall look of web page to make it presentable.
   -> with Css user can Understand the web page content easily by making UI as rich.
   -> History:
         -> CSS invert in W3C(consortium) on 17th dec, 1996 by hackon wiem Lie.
   -> uses
         -> Improves looks.
         -> Separates content and design.
         -> maintains consistancy across multiple pages.
         -> Make web pages as responsive for different types of devices(mobile, tablets, laptop).
         -> Reduce code duplication.
         -> Adds visuals effect like animation, transition , transformation.

How to use CSS?

    selector {
        prop : value;

    }
    -> Selector : targetting HTML element by using its name , id , class.
    -> Declaration block contains one or more Css Declaration Separated by ";".
    _. one declartion contains css property name  and value seperated by ":".
    We can not write duplicate property in same declartion block, if it is so always last occurance will executes.

How Css Works?

-> when CSs loaded into the broweser , tree like struct called CSSOM(Cascading style sheet object model) will be created after parsing css in browser.
-> just like as the browser converts html into a DOM(Document Object Model), it converts css into CSSOM
-> Later browser will combines both DOM and CSSOM to create a render tree.

Types off CSS
   1. Inline Css:
      -> Write css property by using 'style' attribute directly into the html element.
      -> Syntax:
          <h1 style="Color:'blue';font-size:'30px'"></h1>
      -> Advantages:
          - Good for small change.
          - It is having high priority.
      -> Disadvantage:
          - It is requred to apply for each and every html element.
          - Not reusable.

   2. Internal CSS.
      -> write the css property inside <style> tag in the HTML Document.
      -> Advantage:
          - reusable
          - Easy to access.
          - Better for single pages.
    -> Disadventage:
          - Cannot reuse across multiple pages.

   3. External CSS:
      -> Keeping styling property in seperate CSS file.
      -> Can be connected to html using <link> tag.
      -> Advantage:
          - Can be used across multiple web pages.
          - Most recomended.
          - Easy to maintain.      

Box model:
   -> It is an illustraction of box, which wrap around each and every html element.
   -> It is used to maintain space between element.
   -> mainly consider of content, margin, padding and border.
   -> Contents of box model
       1. Content: It is core part box model. it can content of any type like text, image, video, table, form ...
       2. padding: padding goes around content.
         -> It clears the are between content and boreder.
         -> It is transparent in nature.
         -> Applying -ve padding is not possible.
       3. Border: Border goes around content and padding.
         -> it is visible to the user.
       4. Margin: It goes around boreder.
         -> cleare the are between window/ Parent to border.
         -> it can transperent.
         -> Can apply -ve margin.   

Basic selector
  * Tag/name selector:
    targeting an html element bu using its tag name.
    -> Syntax:
        <tag>content</tag>
        # css
            tag{
                // css prop
            }
    
    * Id selector:
        -> selecting an element by writing a "id" attribute, to applying css property.
        -> id should be unique in whole web page.
        -> cannot be duplicated
        -> creating sub id is not allow.
        -> Uses '#' follow by id-name
        -> Syntax:
            # id-name{
                property
            }
        <tag id=id-name>content</tag>

    * class selector:
       -> slecting an elemnt by using"class" to apply css property
       ->class can be duplicated.
       ->creating sub class is allowed
       -> uses'.' to select an class to apply css
       -> Syntax:
          .class-name{
            <tag class="class-name">
          }
  

    * attributes slector:
        ->targeting an html element by using its attributes.
        -> syntax:-
              selector[attributes ="Value"]{
                tag attributes=""
              } 
    
    * Group Selector
        -> targeting two or more selector to apply same css property by using ","(comma seperator)
        -> Syntax:
          sel1, sel2 , sel3, {
            //css prop
          }

    * Universal slector:
        -> Selector all html element on the web pages to apply some css property.
        -> Uses "*" operator
        -> Syntax:
        *{
            property
        }
        -> Commonly used in removing margin from all element and to decide box-sizing.


    * opecity:
       -> applying transparency to an html element.
       -> 0 - 1 - visible
          |
          completely visible

    * Grediant:
       -> Smooth transition between two or more color.
       -> Types:
          1. Linear-gredient
          2. Radiat-gredient
          3. Conic-gredient














